NAMING-COLLISION RESOLUTION (binding decision — Honesty Covenant #2, #7, #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The 0001 prompt's mechanically-generated native target `ConfirmDialog.*` COLLIDES
with an already-shipped sibling surface:

  • 0001 (this prompt) → web `components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx`  = `AiConfirmDialog`
    (AI tool-use approval: tool name + verbatim JSON args + Approve/Cancel).
  • 0012 (shipped)      → web `components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx`  = `ConfirmDialog`
    (destructive-action confirm: severity tint + typed-confirmation gate).

Both prompts declare the identical "Native output: ConfirmDialog.*". The 0012
surface already occupies `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/ConfirmDialog.*`
(commit f5a7add1a, in-tree on this branch). Overwriting it would destroy a
completed sibling surface — a #7 "predecessor bypass" / #2 "scope narrowing"
violation.

RESOLUTION: this AI variant ships as `AiConfirmDialog.*` — matching the web
component's exported symbol name (`export function AiConfirmDialog`) and the
existing `Ai*` native surface convention (AiOutputPanel, AiLimitBanner, ToolCard).
Types are `AiConfirm*`-prefixed, the strings table is "AiConfirmDialog", and the
P1/S11 diagnostics slug is "AiConfirmDialog" — all collision-free with the 0012
`ConfirmDialog` surface, which is left intact and untouched. This mirrors the
collision resolution already adopted for this exact surface on a sibling parallel
branch (commit 2ba5040a5).

